# ATLAS — THE LEARNING LOOP
# =========================
# Install:  crontab -l > /tmp/ct && cat deploy/learning.cron >> /tmp/ct \
#           && crontab /tmp/ct && crontab -l | tail -12
#
# WHY ITS OWN FILE. These two lines were parked in deploy/meridian.cron, which
# installs as a block: adding MERIDIAN would have added an ATLAS job, and removing
# MERIDIAN would have silently removed the path recorder with it. MERIDIAN reads
# nothing from ATLAS and writes nothing to it, and that has to hold in the deploy
# surface as well as in the code.
#
# WHAT THIS LOOP IS. The pipeline records verdicts; this records the evidence
# behind them. Every row in signal_outcomes exits at exactly -1.00R or +2.00R
# because resolution writes the level it crossed as the fill, so no exit rule is
# testable from it -- not a 3R target, not a trailing stop, not a time stop. These
# two jobs write the path and then read it.
#
# THE BOX RUNS UTC. IST = UTC + 5:30, and these are written in UTC.
#
#   13:40 UTC = 19:10 IST
#   13:55 UTC = 19:25 IST
#
# Both run Mon-Fri only. A weekend run would walk the same paths to the same
# answer and write the same rows.

# ── 1. THE PATH RECORDER ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# After the EOD chain has published and update_outcomes has resolved. Walks the
# 20-day forward path of every signal and every detection not already measured,
# from the daily bars on the box -- which is why it runs here and nowhere else.
# Incremental: existing_keys() skips what is already in the table.
#
# The one-off backfill for the existing record, run by hand once:
#   cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && venv/bin/python -m engine.excursions --backfill
40 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.excursions >> /home/ubuntu/logs/excursions.log 2>&1

# ── 2. THE DETECTION HYPOTHESIS ───────────────────────────────────────
# 2,787 of the 2,941 rows in live_signals are intraday detections, published with
# entry, stop and two targets since June, and not one has ever been scored. This
# reads the paths written fifteen minutes earlier and reports what they did, at
# 1.5R / 2R / 3R, with the ambiguous same-bar ties left as a range rather than
# assigned to a side.
#
# REPORT ONLY. It writes nothing, to any table, and is wired to no threshold. The
# output is a log an operator reads; acting on it is a separate decision taken
# once a span longer than seven weeks has accumulated.
55 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.score_live_outcomes >> /home/ubuntu/logs/detection_hypothesis.log 2>&1
